<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9784" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-cerpo</span></b> , psi, ptum, 3, v. a.
		carpo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to pluck, pull</i>, or <i>tear in pieces, to
			rend</i> (rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epistulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 10, 12, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">librum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 55, 11</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Gell. 4, 18, 12</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litteras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folia coronae concerpta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 3, 9, § 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linteolum,</span>”
				<i>lint</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 15, 61, § 216</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">31, 9, 45,
				§ 100</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (acc. to carpo, II. B. b. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>), <i>to abuse, revile,
				censure</i>: Curionem ferventissime, Cael. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 8,
				6, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
